{
  "id": "bigville_action_general",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "depends_on": [],
  "self_load_only": true,
  "description": "bigville R75 (block 393000): THE GENERIC ACTION -- perform an action on N THINGS with Y TOOLS (or none). An ActionSpec is data: it -needs-> a Need per input (kind+qty) and -uses-> a ToolUse per tool (kind). Doing the action opens a Job carrying a per-job copy of that checklist; optionally TIMED (an_tick), producing a BULK material (an_done_bulk) or a DISCRETE tool with quality+wear (an_done_item). an_meet consumes each input one at a time (any N), an_use_tool wears each tool one at a time (any Y, or none), and an_done completes it when all are met -- producing the output and tiring the actor. FORGE, BURN, and ASSEMBLE are all just instances (assemble = using a hammer on two component inputs). No rule names an action; adding one -- any number of inputs, any number of tools -- is a data row. This is the general form the 2-slot ax_do/ax_forge and the special cr_assemble collapse into.",
  "nodes": [],
  "edges": [],
  "productions": [],
  "concepts": [],
